{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560593-v20-abyss-mysticism-and-rites-of-the-blood","id":1560593,"title":"[V20] Abyss Mysticism and Rites of the Blood","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-06-12T20:13:19-07:00","id":1560593,"title":"[V20] Abyss Mysticism and Rites of the Blood","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> Are Abyss Mysticism rituals subject to the <b>The Blood and the Will</b> rule from Rites of the Blood?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rites of the Blood p.130</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Blood and the Will</b><br /> The dice mechanics of Necromancy as<br /> depicted in V20 work somewhat differently<br /> than what is described here, but for the<br /> purposes of this book, <b>Necromancy is just<br /> another form of blood magic and works<br /> mechanically just the same as all of the other<br /> paths, i.e.</b> with Willpower rolls instead of<br /> Attribute + Ability rolls for path powers<br /> and <b>Intelligence + Occult rolls for all<br /> Necromancy rituals.</b> Similarly, Sorcery paths<br /> such as Akhu and Koldunic Sorcery which<br /> previously used different dice pools will<br /> now also use Willpower rolls for all paths.<br /> However, if the Storyteller wishes, characters<br /> using Necromancy or any of those previously<br /> covered schools may instead use the dice<br /> pools listed in V20 or in prior Vampire: The<br /> Masquerade supplements as an optional rule.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I ask because the book itself list Abyss Mysticism as Wits + Occult rolls. There is <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541727-v20-is-abyss-mysticism-mechanically-speaking-a-seperate-discipline\">previous thread</a> that touches tangentially on the unusualness of Abyss Mysticism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-12T22:43:12-07:00","id":1560595,"title":"","content":"Basically we have contradictory rules. I'd suggest asking the ST which they prefer to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-14T11:53:40-07:00","id":1560622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560593-v20-abyss-mysticism-and-rites-of-the-blood#post1560593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> Are Abyss Mysticism rituals subject to the <b>The Blood and the Will</b> rule from Rites of the Blood?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I ask because the book itself list Abyss Mysticism as Wits + Occult rolls. There is <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541727-v20-is-abyss-mysticism-mechanically-speaking-a-seperate-discipline\">previous thread</a> that touches tangentially on the unusualness of Abyss Mysticism.</div> </div> </div> </div>My feeling is that Wits + Occult is used if you don't want to use the unified mechanics in <i>Rites of the Blood</i>, which are optional anyway.<br /> <br /> While other traditions have their own mechanics included in the CRB, Abyss Mysticism doesn't, so it needs those listed somewhere. Also, I note that some Dur-An-Ki rituals are also listed with Wits + Occult in that book\u2014case in point, Blood and Bane, which is literally next to the Abyss Mysticism section on p. 37.<br /> <br /> Ergo, you can choose to use the Wits + Occult or Intelligence+ Occult rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-14T20:40:27-07:00","id":1560630,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I'm not a big fan of the Willpower dice pool anyway, as it's quite limiting to the user and unfair in the system. This is a common complain among people who likes to play &quot;mystically inclided vampires/Blood sorcerers&quot;, if you depend on the basic system (and your ST doesn't give a damn about balancing, that is) you're most of the time in a much worser position when compared to melee fighters, this is something V5 finally kind of fixed, albeit only for really powerful blood magicians as there are finally some balanced options to deal real damage with blood magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-15T08:27:59-07:00","id":1560636,"title":"","content":"Focusing on Willpower for <i>everything</i> is easier than focusing on multiple attributes and skills, in many cases. Depending on the edition, Willpower dots are also quite cheap with freebies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-15T09:28:20-07:00","id":1560637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560593-v20-abyss-mysticism-and-rites-of-the-blood?p=1560636#post1560636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Focusing on Willpower for <i>everything</i> is easier than focusing on multiple attributes and skills, in many cases. Depending on the edition, Willpower dots are also quite cheap with freebies.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the only systematic advantage, that is, that's a way to simplify things, so to speak. But, in the end, it's quite limiting for damage dice pools etc. Not to mention that few ST would easily allow a character to start with, say 10 WP, in any case it's not a very impressive damage pool when we think about it. Jaws of the Dracon used an interesting dicepool that I think would make it a bit better, that is Willpower + Occult. But that's also good to highlight one of the common complains players often share with me, that really &quot;high magical power&quot; sem to only be meant for NPCs in Vampire and I can easily understand how that can feel underwhelming for many.<br /> <br /> Let's talk just a little about one of the main inspirations for Vampire, in Anne's Rice Vampire chronicles when we read about Akasha and the real powerful blood gods, it seems much more fearsome when she burns someone to a crisp than when we talk about physical blows, unfortunately that doesn't hold in the RAW here in Vampire, at most a Lure of Flames can deal 3 damage per turn that is not all that scary. The best way to simulate that kind of thing would be with Way of Fire 2: Combustion that is uinronically the best power Way of Fire has, precisely because it gives us a good damage pool (even though the base difficulty to affect &quot;(un)living things&quot; is 7), unlike vulcanic blast that is the level 5 that deals 3 damage per turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-15T21:53:39-07:00","id":1560648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560593-v20-abyss-mysticism-and-rites-of-the-blood#post1560593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> Are Abyss Mysticism rituals subject to the <b>The Blood and the Will</b> rule from Rites of the Blood?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I ask because the book itself list Abyss Mysticism as Wits + Occult rolls. There is <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541727-v20-is-abyss-mysticism-mechanically-speaking-a-seperate-discipline\">previous thread</a> that touches tangentially on the unusualness of Abyss Mysticism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside discussions over the rule in general, the problem is precisely how unusual Abyss Mysticism is.<br /> <br /> Overall the point is that AM doesn't work like sorcery at all, it isn't meant to. Instead:<br /> <br /> 1. It's &quot;rituals&quot; are mechanically more similar to Combo Disciplines. Most look more like alternative Obtenebration effects powers.<br /> <br /> 2. It's main &quot;costs&quot; are permanent mutations to the Mystic, which is the reason why they're weird and ugly as fuck.<br /> <br /> So while there's no definitive answer, I'd say the particulars of Abyss Mysticism would favor it not following any sorcery rule rather than the opposite. For me it clearly isn't sorcery, but another kind of power, less &quot;follow ritual and it makes magic happen&quot; and more &quot;let the Abyss mutate you into something stranger that can manifest such and such as a result&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}